    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0025" n="[1]" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg1"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Perry.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 5, 1863</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>We hear as yet nothing from her Catholic Majesty’s government concerning the
                    question of maritime jurisdiction. We are frank, direct, and friendly in our
                    attitude towards Spain. I need not say that we do not fear aggression, although
                    we deprecate it.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horatio J. Perry</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c.</hi>,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Madrid.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
